* {{l|eo|enhavi|gloss=to [[contain]], to [[comprise]], to [[include]]}}
{{mid4}}
* {{l|eo|enhavo|gloss=[[contents]], [[table of contents]]}}
* {{l|eo|hava|gloss=[[comfortable]] (not needy); [[well off]]}}
* {{l|eo|havigi|gloss=to [[supply]], to [[provide]]}}
* {{l|eo|havo}}, {{l|eo|havaĵo|gloss=[[possession]]}}
{{mid4}}
* {{l|eo|malhava}}, {{l|eo|senhava|gloss=[[destitute]], [[penniless]]}}
* {{l|eo|malhavi}}, {{l|eo|senhavi|gloss=to [[lack]]}}
* {{l|eo|senhavigi|gloss=to [[deprive]]}}
* {{l|eo|senhaviĝi|gloss=to [[become]] destitute, to [[lose]] everything}}
{{bottom}}

====Usage notes====
'''-hava''' is sometimes used like a suffix meaning "-having". For example, while {{m|eo|barba}} means related to beards in a general way, {{m|eo|barbhava}} specifically means "having a beard".

